# BARD-CPAC-2026

BARD is an after-score prototype: it analyzes a unique human performance and gives it a visible narrative form through story fragments and live visual atmosphere.

The hackathon prototype is still here, but the new cloud-ready code starts in `src/bard_core`.

## Current Goal

Run the existing idea with a cleaner architecture:

```text
audio
-> emotional/music-feature segmentation
-> coherent story fragments
-> Processing display via OSC
```

## Recommended First Run

Install Python dependencies:

```powershell
py -3.12 -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install -e ".[api,cloud,local-ai]"
```

If `py` is not available on your machine, install Python and use `python -m venv .venv`.

Start the Processing sketch in:

```text
apps/processing/bard_story_visuals
```

Then run the prototype-compatible pipeline:

```powershell
python -m bard_core run-local --audio data/audio/audio.mp3 --audio-provider clap --story-provider local --send-osc
```

For the GCP/Vertex path:

```powershell
python -m bard_core run-local --audio data/audio/audio.mp3 --audio-provider gemini --story-provider vertex --send-osc
```

Private env files are supported with `--env-file` before the command name.

## Docs

- `docs/architecture.md`: code structure and target architecture.
- `docs/gcp_setup.md`: GCP project, service account, keys outside the repo, Docker, and Cloud Run.
- `docs/project_structure.md`: where code, data, examples, and legacy files now live.
- `configs/local.example.env`: local environment template.

## Processing OSC Contract

The Python pipeline sends:

```text
/config/duration <float seconds>
/segment <string mood> <string text>
/start
```

Allowed moods:

```text
ENERGETIC, SOLO, CALM, DEEP, DISSONANT, ANXIOUS
```
